<title>USA: Fannie Mae sets about $1.1 bln REMIC 1997-G5.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae sets about $1.1 bln REMIC 1997-G5.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae said it issued $1,116,200,000 of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities via Bear Stearns.</p>
<p>REMIC trust 1997-G5 is backed by 30-year 8.0 percent Government National Mortgage Association (Ginnie Mae) certificates and various Fannie Mae REMIC tranches. The issue has a settlement date of June 30, the agency said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1562 ))</p>
